{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/pulls/17493","id":4078144474,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJmmzGc7zE4va","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/17493","diff_url":"https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/17493.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vercel/ai/pull/17493.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/issues/17493","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/pulls/17493/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/pulls/17493/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/issues/17493/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/statuses/294db3739a3de30adf82d836876f2296e9d2ad44","number":17493,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(ai): use injective serialization for tool approval HMAC payload","user":{"login":"dnukumamras","id":23266464,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMjY2NDY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23266464?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras","html_url":"https://github.com/dnukumamras","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dnukumamras/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The tool approval signature payload was built by joining fields with `\\n`. Because fields like `toolName` and `toolCallId` can contain a newline, two different field tuples could serialize to identical bytes — so a signature issued for one tuple could verify against a different one. The payload is now serialized with `JSON.stringify` (with a constant domain-separation prefix), which escapes delimiter/control characters and makes the encoding injective.\n\nVerification stays backwards compatible: it falls back to the old newline format only when no signed field contains a `\\n`, so approvals signed by an older version still verify across an upgrade. This legacy fallback is marked `TODO: remove in v8`.\n\n**Happy path**\n- A valid approval signs and verifies for its own `(approvalId, toolCallId, toolName, input)` tuple.\n- Input key ordering is still normalized, so equivalent inputs produce the same signature.\n- A signature in the old newline format still verifies (delimiter-free fields), so a pending approval that straddles an upgrade is not rejected.\n\n**Unhappy path**\n- A tuple whose `toolName` contains a newline can no longer be retupled into `toolCallId` to reuse the same signature for a different tool — in both the new and the legacy fallback paths.\n- Any delimiter/control character (`\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t`, `\\0`, `\"`, `\\\\`) shifted across a field boundary fails verification.\n- A legacy signature over a newline-bearing field no longer verifies (the fallback is refused when a field contains `\\n`).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #17832","labels":[{"id":11443094032,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJmmzGc8AAAACqg_CEA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/labels/task-merge-tracking-no-issue","name":"task-merge-tracking-no-issue","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":11472677924,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJmmzGc8AAAACq9MsJA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/ai/labels/task-bugfix-review-approved","name":"task-bugfix-review-approved","description":null,"color":"ededed","default":f